        -:  370:     * It returns the quote character as a single character string for a given input wrapee
        -:  371:     * string.  If the wrappee does not need to be quoted, the return value is "" (the null
        -:  372:     * string), such as when there are no delimiters in the input wrapee string.  If you want
        -:  373:     * the quote_char to be assuredly not "", then pass in "(" as the wrappee.
        -:  374:     * <p>
